├── contracts/      # Contract CRUD, overlap validation, period search
├── schedules/      # Working schedules, schedule lines, weekly hours computation
├── attendance/     # Check-in/out, worked hours calculation, corrections
└── timeoff/        # Leave types, allocations, transactional leave approvals
```

### 📋 Dev 1 Task Breakdown & Endpoints

#### Task 1.1: Authentication & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
- [ ] **Data Model**: `User` (`id`, `email`, `passwordHash`, `role`, `employeeId`, `isActive`).
- [ ] **Endpoints**:
  - `POST /api/auth/register` (Admin/Seed only) - hash password with `bcrypt.hash(password, 10)`.
  - `POST /api/auth/login` - validate email, compare password, sign JWT with `{ sub: userId, role, employeeId }` (8h expiry).
- [ ] **Middlewares**:
  - `authenticateJWT`: Verifies `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, attaches `req.user`.
  - `authorizeRoles(...roles)`: Enforces roles (`ADMIN`, `HR_MANAGER`, `HR_PAYROLL_USER`, `HR_PAYROLL_MANAGER`, `EMPLOYEE`).
  - `employeeScope`: Ensures `EMPLOYEE` role can only access/modify their own records (`req.user.employeeId`).

#### Task 1.2: Working Schedule Module
- [ ] **Data Models**: `WorkingSchedule` + `ScheduleLine` (`dayOfWeek`, `startTime`, `endTime`, `breakMinutes`).
- [ ] **Endpoints**:
  - `POST /api/schedules` (create schedule + nested `ScheduleLine[]` in one request).
  - `GET /api/schedules` & `GET /api/schedules/:id`.
  - `PUT /api/schedules/:id` & `DELETE /api/schedules/:id`.
- [ ] **Business Rule**: Compute `calculateWeeklyHours(scheduleId)` dynamically as $\sum(\text{endTime} - \text{startTime} - \text{breakMinutes})$ on every `GET` response. Never store it statically.

#### Task 1.3: Employee Master Module
- [ ] **Data Model**: `Employee` (`firstName`, `lastName`, `email`, `phone`, `jobPosition`, `department`, `status`, `managerId`, `scheduleId`, `bankName`, `accountNumber`).
- [ ] **Endpoints**:
  - `POST /api/employees` (HR Manager+).
  - `GET /api/employees` (supports `?view=kanban` or `?view=list`, query filters by `department`, `status`, `search`).
  - `GET /api/employees/:id` & `PATCH /api/employees/:id`.
  - **Smart Button Routes**:
    - `GET /api/employees/:id/contracts`
    - `GET /api/employees/:id/attendance`
    - `GET /api/employees/:id/timeoff`
    - `GET /api/employees/:id/allocations`

#### Task 1.4: Contract Management Module
- [ ] **Data Model**: `Contract` (`employeeId`, `salaryStructureId`, `wage`, `startDate`, `endDate`, `status`, `department`, `jobPosition`).
- [ ] **Endpoints**:
  - `POST /api/contracts` & `GET /api/contracts` & `PATCH /api/contracts/:id`.
  - `PATCH /api/contracts/:id/activate` (auto-expires any previous active contract for the employee).
  - `GET /api/contracts/lookup?employeeId=&periodStart=&periodEnd=` (helper for Dev 2's Payroll Engine).
- [ ] **Business Rule**: `assertNoOverlappingActiveContract()` - reject creation/activation if dates overlap with an existing `ACTIVE` contract.

#### Task 1.5: Attendance Module
- [ ] **Data Model**: `Attendance` (`employeeId`, `date`, `checkIn`, `checkOut`, `workedHours`, `status`, `correctedBy`, `correctionNotes`).
- [ ] **Endpoints**:
  - `POST /api/attendance/check-in` & `POST /api/attendance/:id/check-out` (computes `workedHours` on the fly).
  - `GET /api/attendance` (filter by `employeeId`, `dateRange`, `status`).
  - `PATCH /api/attendance/:id/correct` (HR Manager+ only: updates times, sets `status = 'CORRECTED'`, logs `correctedBy`).
- [ ] **Business Rule**: Automatically flag missing check-outs after end-of-day as `EXCEPTION`.

#### Task 1.6: Time Off & Allocations Module
- [ ] **Data Models**: `TimeOffType`, `LeaveAllocation`, `LeaveRequest`.
- [ ] **Endpoints**:
  - `POST /api/timeoff/types` & `GET /api/timeoff/types` (Admin/HR Manager).
  - `POST /api/timeoff/allocations` & `GET /api/timeoff/allocations` (computed `remaining = allocated - taken`).
  - `POST /api/timeoff/requests` (Employee creates for self, HR creates for anyone).
  - `PATCH /api/timeoff/requests/:id/approve` & `PATCH /api/timeoff/requests/:id/refuse`.
- [ ] **Business Rule (Prisma Transaction)**: On approval:
  1. Set request status to `APPROVED`.
  2. Find employee's matching `LeaveAllocation`.
  3. Validate `taken + duration <= allocated`.
  4. Increment `taken` by `duration`. Both writes must succeed or roll back.

